%% The lifecycle of one confirmation_prompt, as core/confirmation/machine.ts
%% implements it. One registry keyed by confirm token; every arrow is a pure
%% function of (registry, event). Taking the lock is the transition out of live.
%%{init: {"layout": "dagre", "themeVariables": {"fontSize": "17px"}}}%%
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> live: prompt valid, its answer finished
    [*] --> void: its answer was cut, failed or stopped

    live --> confirming: confirm() takes the lock, synchronously
    live --> expired: deadline on the server clock
    live --> superseded: newer prompt, same action
    live --> void: user switched, new conversation

    confirming --> confirmed: 200
    confirming --> expired: 410
    confirming --> superseded: 409 token_superseded
    confirming --> rejected: 403, 409, 422
    confirming --> reconciling: no response

    reconciling --> confirmed: status used
    reconciling --> live: status live, nothing ran
    reconciling --> expired: status expired
    reconciling --> superseded: status superseded
    reconciling --> rejected: status void, invalid
    reconciling --> unresolved: status unreachable

    unresolved --> reconciling: Check again

    note left of unresolved
        Unknown outcome. The card offers
        "Check again", never a second Confirm.
    end note

    note right of live
        Not a state of the machine but a rule of the store:
        while any answer is still streaming, no prompt can be
        confirmed. The server may already have replaced the token.
    end note
